Fix DPD service surviving reverse-to-despatch, block despatch on an
unavailable saved service, keep shipping fields editable until invoiced (v0.103)

Reverse to Despatch no longer clears the chosen DPD service:
- OrderReversalService.reverseToDespatch() was clearing dpdNetworkKey
  alongside the actual DPD booking fields it's undoing (consignment/parcel
  numbers, shipped-at). Clearing the service too meant the next despatch
  found nothing explicitly chosen and silently auto-picked whatever DPD's
  live lookup returned first - reported as a Parcel Next Day order coming
  back as a Pre-12 (or similar) after reversing and re-shipping.
- The DPD booking itself is still fully undone on reversal exactly as
  before; only the staff member's own Service choice now survives it.
  cancelAndReturnToStock() (a full cancellation back to On Hold, not the
  reported scenario) still clears it, since that's genuinely a fresh
  release cycle.

Despatch now refuses to proceed if the saved service isn't available:
- DespatchService.confirmDespatch() calls a new
  DpdShippingService.assertOrderServiceAvailable() right at the start,
  before any stock movement or status change - if the order's explicitly
  chosen service isn't actually available (or DPD can't even be asked),
  the whole despatch is rejected and nothing moves. Everything else about
  DPD booking (bookDpdShipment(), further down) stays best-effort exactly
  as before - this is deliberately the one case that's a hard stop, per
  the explicit ask.
- Skipped when no service was ever explicitly chosen (existing auto-pick
  fallback still applies) or a shipment's already booked for the order.
- No frontend change needed for the "error with a back button" part - both
  Split and Serial Packing already show a top-level error banner and
  already have a permanent "← Back to Despatch" link above the packing
  grid; this now just reaches them via a real validation failure instead
  of never firing before despatch had already gone through.

Shipping cost/courier/service editable for an order's whole life, until invoiced:
- Order Edit no longer restricts these to the On Hold release form - they
  now stay editable (open the order, change them, click Save Order) at any
  status right up until the order's delivery has actually been invoiced
  (Order.shippingInvoiced, from v0.102), at which point the screen locks
  them to a read-only summary instead.
- OrderRequest/OrderService.applyFields carry dpdNetworkKey now too (only
  releaseForDespatch could set it before), and OrderService.update()
  rejects a genuine change to any of the three once shippingInvoiced is
  true - enforced server-side, not just hidden in the UI.
- Covers the reported scenario directly: an order released on one service,
  changed by staff before despatch after a customer calls to switch, and
  despatch/packing picks up whatever's saved at confirmation time - not
  what was chosen at release.

Written and reviewed without a working compiler in this environment
(Maven Central/npm registry both blocked here) - please build and
smoke-test before relying on this, particularly: reversing an order to
despatch and re-shipping keeps the original service; a despatch with a
now-unavailable saved service is cleanly blocked and rolls back; and
shipping cost/courier/service can be changed and saved after release, then
lock once actually invoiced.

